course: dictionary
lesson: 1892
title: The colon
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A colon (:) is a punctuation mark that tells the reader that something is coming. The words before it must be a complete sentence that could stand alone. «You will need three things: a pen, a ruler and glue.» The colon introduces the list.
explain: Look at the words after the colon. They explain, list or give an example of what came before. If the words before the colon are not a whole sentence, the colon is probably doing a different job, such as showing time or a ratio.
explain: Colons also appear in numbers. A clock time like «7:30» and a ratio like 2:3 use a colon, but they do not join sentences. A ratio is read «two to three», and the colon is just a way to write it.
fact: A colon is written as :, with one dot above another dot.
fact: A colon comes after a complete sentence and introduces a list, an explanation or an example.
fact: A digital clock shows the hour before the colon and the minutes after it, so 06:05 is five past six.
fact: In a ratio such as 2:3, the colon is read as «to», so 2:3 is «two to three».
fact: In the body, the colon is the large intestine (large bowel), the tube where water is taken out of food waste.
exercise: «You will need three things: a pen, a ruler and glue.» What job does the colon do here? | It joins two words into one | *It introduces a list | It ends the sentence like a full stop
exercise: What time is shown by 06:05 on a digital clock? | Five o'clock exactly | Six hours and five minutes | *Five minutes past six | Six minutes past five
exercise: How do you read the colon in the ratio 2:3? | Two plus three | Two colon three | *Two to three | Twenty-three
test: Which part must come before a colon? | A number only | *A complete sentence | A single word | A question mark
test: In the body, what is the colon? | The heart | A bone in the leg | The mouth | *The large intestine, also called the large bowel
exam: Which sentence uses the colon correctly? | Bread, milk and eggs: the shop sells. | *The shop sells three things: bread, milk and eggs. | The shop sells three things bread, milk: and eggs. | The shop: sells bread milk and eggs.
